<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Same-week ophthalmology consultation for new distortion and reduced acuity in the left eye, with OCT and fluorescein or OCT angiography as needed. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024) [S]</item><item>Intravitreal aflibercept 2 mg in the left eye every four weeks for three doses, then treat-and-extend by two-week steps while the macula stays dry. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024) [S]</item><item>At each injection visit: best-corrected acuity, OCT, and intraocular pressure before and after injection; teach warning signs of endophthalmitis and retinal detachment. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026) [S]</item><item>Start an AREDS2 supplement (vitamin C 500 mg, vitamin E 400 IU, lutein 10 mg, zeaxanthin 2 mg, zinc 80 mg, copper 2 mg daily) for intermediate AMD in the right eye; no beta-carotene. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024) [S]</item><item>Daily home Amsler grid checks for each eye, with same-day calls for new distortion; dilated examination of the right eye at each retina visit. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024) [S]</item><item>Low-vision rehabilitation: task lighting, magnification, high-contrast marking, home fall-risk review, and a driving assessment. Guideline: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026) [S]</item><item>Repeat the PHQ-2 at follow-up because vision loss raises the risk of depression. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to ophthalmology, Yuki Tanabe, MD, ordered 1968-03-10 [S]</item></list></text>

